HanaNakamura: Hello dear, it is a pleasure to meet you! Where do you come from? I have never seen you around here.
David: Hello, Misses...?
HanaNakamura: Hana. Hana Nakamura.
David: Interesting name. Do you know what it stands for? 
HanaNakamura: It is a quite traditional japanese name. Hana means flower and nakamura means something like "village in the middle"
David: Wow. Beautiful!
David: My name is David. It originates from Hebrew and means "the loved one"!
HanaNakamura: [wave]hihi[/wave] That is something beautiful too! 
HanaNakamura: I hope you have a great time here in Narai-juku. 
HanaNakamura: But you have to watch out: For a few days now some samurai soldiers settled down. 
HanaNakamura: They look so aggressive. I cant calm them down with tea or anything!
David: No worries, I know how to watch out for myself!
